1
00:00:02,790 --> 00:00:06,300
OK. Today's topic:
how to "idle" on a unicycle.

2
00:00:06,366 --> 00:00:18,918
[Music]

3
00:00:18,984 --> 00:00:22,038
To "idle" on a unicycle,
you don't need much space.

4
00:00:22,104 --> 00:00:24,110
But you do need a unicycle.

5
00:00:27,194 --> 00:00:30,479
The thing is, on a unicycle,

6
00:00:30,545 --> 00:00:32,038
you can't really stay completely still,

7
00:00:32,104 --> 00:00:35,388
so you do half-turns of the wheel
to stay balanced.

8
00:00:35,454 --> 00:00:38,834
The wheel goes once in front of you,
then once behind you.

9
00:00:39,334 --> 00:00:44,512
Unlike when you ride normally,
you don't stay over the wheel.

10
00:00:44,578 --> 00:00:48,200
When I ride forward, my body
always stays over the wheel,

11
00:00:48,266 --> 00:00:50,380
and I lean forward a little.

12
00:00:54,224 --> 00:00:58,527
The wheel goes once in front of you
and once behind you.

13
00:00:58,593 --> 00:01:01,323
It's as if your body
were split at the hips.

14
00:01:01,823 --> 00:01:04,318
And the upper body, the shoulders,
stay in place.

15
00:01:04,384 --> 00:01:07,790
Only the legs and the wheel
go forward and back.

16
00:01:12,331 --> 00:01:16,157
As for the feet,
it's a half-turn of the wheel every time.

17
00:01:16,223 --> 00:01:22,890
Here, it does half-turns,
from front to back.

18
00:01:27,283 --> 00:01:33,780
My right foot goes back once,
forward, back, forward, back...

19
00:01:35,963 --> 00:01:39,755
It's not that hard a trick,
but it's not your usual position,

20
00:01:39,821 --> 00:01:44,520
so it takes a bit of practice.

21
00:01:48,023 --> 00:01:50,670
To practice, the best thing
is to hold on to a wall.

22
00:01:52,593 --> 00:01:55,630
I hold on to the wall
and do the trick.

23
00:01:57,178 --> 00:01:58,705
And I let go when I can...

24
00:01:59,205 --> 00:02:00,671
...and grab it again.

25
00:02:01,273 --> 00:02:03,032
To land this trick,

26
00:02:03,098 --> 00:02:05,163
it takes a bit of practice.

27
00:02:05,663 --> 00:02:08,764
At first, don't be shy about holding on,
and spend time doing it.

28
00:02:09,264 --> 00:02:13,698
Then let go, and grab the wall
again when you need to.

29
00:02:13,764 --> 00:02:16,274
Try to keep the motion going
so you get used to it.

30
00:02:16,774 --> 00:02:20,174
Once you've got it,
try doing it without the wall.

31
00:02:20,674 --> 00:02:22,632
Once you're a bit used to the trick,

32
00:02:22,698 --> 00:02:26,690
you can try it straight from riding,
if you have room at home.

33
00:02:26,769 --> 00:02:33,188
[Music]

34
00:02:33,254 --> 00:02:35,320
First, just once.

35
00:02:38,494 --> 00:02:40,040
Then twice.

36
00:02:45,074 --> 00:02:48,580
And so on: three, four, five times,
until you're comfortable.

37
00:02:51,574 --> 00:02:54,048
One variation
is to do it while turning.

38
00:02:54,114 --> 00:02:56,594
If every time I pedal forward,

39
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:59,640
I go left, for example,
I'll end up turning left.

40
00:02:59,693 --> 00:03:07,684
[Music]

41
00:03:07,684 --> 00:03:11,654
If every time I do a half-turn
of the pedals, forward or back,

42
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:13,278
I go right or left,

43
00:03:13,344 --> 00:03:18,660
always the same side,
and I crab sideways a little.

44
00:03:18,749 --> 00:03:25,907
[Music]

45
00:03:25,907 --> 00:03:28,636
For the more adventurous,
you can take the top foot off

46
00:03:29,136 --> 00:03:33,420
since it isn't doing much anyway,
and do a "one-foot idle".

47
00:03:33,746 --> 00:03:44,734
[Music]

48
00:03:44,734 --> 00:03:49,442
As always, use a wall
as much as you can,

49
00:03:49,508 --> 00:03:53,980
a pole, whatever you've got,
and practice, practice, practice.

50
00:03:57,129 --> 00:04:00,233
Once you get it, it opens up
lots of other "idles". There are tons!

51
00:04:00,299 --> 00:04:02,193
Every "idle" works the same way:

52
00:04:02,259 --> 00:04:05,540
the body stays still,
only the wheel moves forward and back.

53
00:04:05,639 --> 00:04:28,771
[Music]

54
00:04:28,771 --> 00:04:30,380
Good luck and see you soon!
